## Dataset

This project uses the **Twitter Hate Speech Detection** dataset from Kaggle.

The dataset is designed for the task of identifying hate speech in tweets. For this project, hate speech is defined as tweets containing **racist** or **sexist** content.

Each tweet is assigned one of the following labels:

| Label | Description                            |
| ----- | -------------------------------------- |
| 0     | Non-hate speech (No racism or sexism)  |
| 1     | Hate speech (Racist or sexist content) |

### Dataset Statistics

* **Total Tweets:** 31,962
* **Training Data:** Labeled tweets used for model training and evaluation
* **Task Type:** Binary Text Classification

### Objective

Given a collection of tweets and their corresponding labels, the goal is to build a machine learning model that can automatically classify whether a tweet contains racist or sexist content.

This dataset presents a real-world text classification challenge, including issues such as noisy social media text, informal language, and class imbalance.

**Dataset Source:**
https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/arkhoshghalb/twitter-sentiment-analysis-hatred-speech
